XNNPACK: no KleidiAI pf32 SME2 GEMM and no x32 SME2 LHS packing on Apple
(macOS and iOS). patch_c_api.sh section 21.

On SME2 CPUs (Apple M4/M5 measured) the pf32 SME2 f32 GEMM gives results
that depend on the thread count. At 4 threads (LiteRT-LM's default) sessions
differ by up to 2.5 nat per token; other thread counts repeat a wrong answer;
on some models 1 thread is off too. Skipping only these three SME2 branches
gives one result at 1/4/12 threads on every affected model
(doc/research/macos-cpu-nondeterminism-0.19.md on research/
macos-cpu-nondeterminism-0.19). The three go together: the pf32 kernels
expect an LHS packed by the matching pack-lh config, and either alone
gives garbage. On Apple the SME (non-2) branches that follow are used instead.

Upstream: google/XNNPACK#11789 (also google-ai-edge/LiteRT-LM#4145).
Drop this when XNNPACK fixes #11789: re-run the scorerep probe at 1/4/12
threads on an SME2 Mac without it. When the XNNPACK pin moves, the fetch fails
(tensorflow_xnnpack_patch_file.patch names the pinned archive) until this is
re-checked against the new pin.
Against XNNPACK 28d1fc6d908bc4d80920be989177b7eb1a4aebc8, strip 1.

